From f9422ec2636600b6fa53facb727c31f42455d85d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gambuzino24 <gambuzino24@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:18:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support Ninja Gaiden II shaders

- memory export (eA/eM#) to guest memory through a buffer device address,
  after Xenia's SPIR-V translator (NG2 skins on the GPU with it)
- vertex shaders get the vertex index in r0.x, as on the hardware
- vertex fetches without a declared element read guest memory through the
  vertex fetch constants; full fetches latch the index for mini fetches
- bool constants addressed like the hardware (256 bits, VS 0-127, PS 128-255)
- bool-conditional exec blocks (cexec) are conditional; CondExecPredCleanEnd
  ends the shader
- 32 texture fetch slots, generic names for slots without reflection data,
  1D textures (with offset) sampled as Nx1 2D textures
- vertex shaders sample mip 0 (no implicit LOD outside pixel shaders)
- NG2 vertex input locations (up to four position/normal streams) when
  UNLEASHED_RECOMP is not defined; unmapped semantics are an error
- 8-byte aligned 64-bit constant loads (Vulkan validation)
- SPIR-V compile failures are fatal in release builds

The DXIL (D3D12) path is not updated for the new shared constant layout.
